    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primera-junta">Primera Junta</a> swore loyalty to the captive Ferdinand VII but refused the authority of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s Council of Regency, and historians still debate whether the &quot;Mask of Ferdinand&quot; hid independence as the goal from the start.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assembly-of-the-year-xiii">Assembly of the Year XIII</a> freed the children of slaves, abolished the Inquisition, torture, noble ranks and the mit'a, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/encomienda">encomienda</a> and yanaconazgo, and approved the anthem and arms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>, yet rejected Artigas's deputies and their demand for independence and federalism.</li><li>On 9 July 1816 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-tucuman">Congress of Tucumán</a> declared independence from Ferdinand VII, his successors and metropole, in Spanish, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quechua">Quechua</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aymara">Aymara</a>; San Martín's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a> then won Chacabuco and Maipú, while at home the Directory fell to the federal caudillos at Cepeda in 1820.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-belgrano">Manuel Belgrano</a> raised the new light blue and white flag at Rosario in 1812 without asking; the First Triumvirate ordered him to hide it and sent him a Spanish red and yellow one, but he had already left for the north and never received the message.</p></aside>
    </section>

